  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 315 AM EST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nLong range models depict reinforcing high pressure and drier \nconditions prevailing across the area during the weekend in the wake \nof a dry FROPA. Mainly single-digit POPs are expected each day \nthrough Sunday. \n\nFor early next week, models depict a potential mid-lvl trough moving \nacross the area and bringing increasing chances of showers for the \nlate Monday-Tuesday timeframe. But even so, max POPs seem to remain \nin the 20-30% range. \n\nThe latest trend in guidance is also to bring a more pronounced \ntemperature response as overall northerly flow develops in the \nwake of the FROPA. Afternoon highs should remain in the upper 70s \nto low 80s by early next week.",
